# Copy to .env.local to override. Vite only exposes variables prefixed VITE_.

# Where the API lives, for the dev and preview servers only. It is read by
# vite.config.js when it answers /config.js — it is NOT substituted into the
# bundle, and nothing in CI sets it.
#
# That is the point of the arrangement: the built artifact names no host, and
# production learns its API from /config.js, which the deploy writes on the
# server from FRONTEND_API_URL in /opt/dnd/.env. Moving the API is an env var
# and a re-run, not a rebuild.
#
# Defaults to http://localhost:8000, which is what `just dev` serves. The dev
# (5173) and preview (4173) ports are already in the API's CORS_ORIGINS, and the
# session needs that: the API is a different origin, so every request goes out
# with credentials, which a browser only allows against an origin the API names.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
